# AI Voice Calling Agent — Core Rules

Production-grade SaaS. Documentation: `docs/README.md`

## Docs by layer
- Backend: `docs/backend/` — API, database, voice, AI
- Frontend: `docs/frontend/` — dashboard, UI, React Query
- Shared: `docs/shared/` — system architecture, roadmaps, general rules

## Stack
- Frontend: Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, ShadCN, TanStack Query, React Hook Form, Zod
- Backend: Express, TypeScript, Prisma, JWT + refresh + RBAC
- DB: PostgreSQL (NeoDB/Neon). Telephony: Exotel. Queue: BullMQ + Redis

## Non-negotiables
1. Never change existing business logic unless explicitly requested
2. TypeScript only — no JavaScript, no mocks/placeholders/demo code
3. Clean architecture: Route → Validator → Controller → Service → Repository → Prisma
4. No business logic in controllers; no raw fetch in React components
5. Before coding: analyze architecture, deps, folder structure, schema; list affected files
6. Complete implementations only; preserve backward compatibility

## API base
All REST endpoints under `/api/v1`.

## Priorities
Scalability, security, maintainability, performance, UX, production readiness.
